Generate one complete Modelica model for this requirement:
Create an instrumented closed-chain robotic mechanism named PantographDriveD. Preserve these measurements and their roles: Measure actuator state, output pose, and every loop-closure residual. The measured plant is defined by this embodiment: A fixed parallelogram uses 0.25 m and 0.50 m links, six revolute Z joints, and one prismatic input with 0.16 m travel. One bounded linear actuator commands the input coordinate, limited to 320 N. The requested behavior is to drive the designated input at constant speed and observe the coupled output motion. Use gravity where applicable and prevent nonadjacent link collision. Use PI input-speed control with command saturation and apply a controlled 8 N-or-N.m load disturbance during the middle third. Run at 200 Hz for 14 s and retain synchronized state, command, and sensor traces. Require actuator bounds, speed band, every closure error, output travel, and valid joint references, primary tracking error below 0.002 m closure after 9.1 s, and no NaN or infinite physical, control, or estimator values. Treat facts not stated in this request as unknown rather than inventing them.

